Based on these details, your task is to determine whether the provided code snippet contains the bug.
Think step by step.
Be conservative in your assessment. If you are unsure, answer "no."

Root cause:
A race condition between `nvme_poll_irqdisable()` and `nvme_reset_work()` that calls `nvme_dev_disable()`. In `nvme_poll_irqdisable()`, `pci_irq_vector()` is called twice – once for `disable_irq()` and once for `enable_irq()`. If between these two calls, `nvme_dev_disable()` sets `pdev->msix_enabled = 0`, the second `pci_irq_vector()` will return a different IRQ number (INTx instead of MSI-X). This leads to an attempt to enable an IRQ that was never disabled, causing an IRQ warning and potentially unbalanced interrupt handling.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>disable_irq(pci_irq_vector(pdev, nvmeq->cq_vector));</text>
<text>enable_irq(pci_irq_vector(pdev, nvmeq->cq_vector));</text>

Reason:
The `pci_irq_vector()` call is made twice, once for `disable_irq()` and once for `enable_irq()`. If between these two calls another task (e.g., `nvme_reset_work` calling `nvme_dev_disable()`) sets `pdev->msix_enabled = 0`, the second `pci_irq_vector()` may return a different IRQ number (INTx instead of MSI-X). This causes `enable_irq()` to attempt enabling an IRQ that was never disabled by the first call, leading to an unbalanced IRQ warning and possible system instability.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>irq = pci_irq_vector(pdev, nvmeq->cq_vector);</text>
<text>disable_irq(irq);</text>
<text>enable_irq(irq);</text>

Reason:
By saving the IRQ number into the local variable `irq` before any disable/enable operations, both `disable_irq()` and `enable_irq()` use the same IRQ number regardless of any concurrent changes to `pdev->msix_enabled`. This ensures balanced interrupt handling even if `pci_free_irq_vectors()` frees the IRQ concurrently, as `disable_irq()` and `enable_irq()` on a stale IRQ number are still valid and safe.


Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:
{
	struct pci_dev *pdev = to_pci_dev(nvmeq->dev->dev);
	int irq;

	WARN_ON_ONCE(test_bit(NVMEQ_POLLED, &nvmeq->flags));

	irq = pci_irq_vector(pdev, nvmeq->cq_vector);
	disable_irq(irq);
	spin_lock(&nvmeq->cq_poll_lock);
	nvme_poll_cq(nvmeq, NULL);
	spin_unlock(&nvmeq->cq_poll_lock);
	enable_irq(irq);
}

